/**
\fn pdg::Animated::changeSpinTo(number radiansPerSecond, number durationSeconds, int easing)
\brief Animate the spin rate to a target.

Uses clockwise radians per second. Duration is the time to reach the new rate, not the lifetime of the motion: the final rate continues until changed or stopped. Dynamic PhysicsBody owners reject this operation. Durations are explicit floating-point seconds. Zero applies immediately; a request after wait() or andThen() must have positive duration.

\param radiansPerSecond Angular rate in clockwise radians per second.
\param durationSeconds Finite nonnegative duration in seconds.
\param easing Integer easing constant; elapsed time and duration use seconds.

\return This object, for chaining.

\see setSpin(), changeSpinBy()
*/
